This code is a complete, compilable C program that fulfills the user's request. It uses the pigpio library to control a submersible water pump connected to GPIO18, and the MCP3008 SPI ADC with CE0 on GPIO8. It logs every moisture reading and pump activation/deactivation with timestamps to 'irrigation.log'. It accepts command-line options to configure the moisture threshold, pump duration, and sleep interval. It gracefully handles SPI errors with up to 3 retries per read. On SIGINT or SIGTERM, it shuts off the pump, closes the SPI channel, terminates pigpio, and exits cleanly. It ensures the pump is turned off on all exit paths, including SPI open failure.

