        } else if (frequency > MAX_FREQUENCY) {
            frequency = MAX_FREQUENCY;
        }

        printf("Distance: %d, Blink frequency: %d\n", distance, frequency);

        led_state = !led_state;
        gpioWrite(GPIO_LED, led_state);

        usleep(1000000 / frequency);
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This code initializes the GPIO and I2C interfaces, sets up the shutdown handler, and enters a loop where it reads the distance from the sensor, calculates the blink frequency, and blinks the LED. If the I2C read fails, it retries up to 3 times before giving up and shutting down. The LED blinks smoothly because each loop iteration performs one half-cycle of the blink. The distance and blink frequency are logged to stdout. The code checks every pigpio and I2C call, and handles the sensor-absent and bus-error paths gracefully.

