This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and starts a periodic measurement. It then enters a loop where it polls the sensor for a data ready status, reads the measurement when data is ready, validates the CRC-8 checksum, stores the measurement in a circular buffer, prints the measurement, and sets the state of an LED based on the CO2 level. On exit, it stops the periodic measurement, closes the I2C handle, releases the GPIO, and terminates the pigpio library.

