This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the I2C bus. It sends a 2-byte command to the SDP810 sensor, waits 45 ms, then reads 9 bytes of data. It validates the CRC of each data field, converts the raw readings, and logs the timestamp, pressure in Pa, and temperature in Celsius to a CSV file once per second. It gracefully handles I2C errors and CRC failures by logging the error and continuing with the next reading. It also handles SIGINT (usually from Ctrl+C) by closing the I2C handle, terminating the pigpio daemon, closing the log file, and exiting cleanly.

