This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up GPIO4 as an input with a pull-up resistor, and handles the DHT22 1-wire protocol. It sends a start signal by pulling the data line low for at least 1 ms, then reads the 40-bit response. It parses the data, validates the 8-bit checksum, and posts the readings as a JSON payload to http://yourserver.com/api/humidity. It handles sensor-absent, checksum, and network errors gracefully with up to 3 retries. It ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including signal handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

