This code is a complete, compilable C program that fulfils the user's request. It uses the pigpio library for GPIO handling and I2C read/write operations, and the standard C library for file handling and time operations. It includes error checking for every init and syscall, handles errors by closing the I2C handle and releasing pigpio resources, and implements a clean exit on SIGINT. It also implements a falling-edge ISR on GPIO4 with an internal pull-up to toggle logging on and off, debouncing in the ISR using pigpio tick comparison. It reads the BMP180 calibration coefficients from registers 0xAA-0xBE, validates them, and uses oversampling OSS=3 for pressure measurements with the correct 26 ms conversion delay. It implements the full Bosch BMP180 compensation algorithm using integer arithmetic, with no floating-point pow calls. It logs only when logging is enabled, and when disabled, it prints a status message. It samples every 2 seconds.

