This code assumes that the I2C device is already enabled and configured. It also assumes that the I2C bus is named "/dev/i2c-1". If the I2C bus is different, you will need to adjust the open() call accordingly.

Please note that the i2c_smbus_read_word_data function is used for simplicity, but it only works for I2C devices that support SMBus protocol. For devices that do not support SMBus, you will need to use the i2c_rdwr system call directly.

Also, this code does not handle the case where the CSV file cannot be written to. If the file permissions are not set correctly, the fopen() call will fail and the program will exit.

