This code initializes the GPIO and sets up the cleanup function for SIGINT and SIGTERM. It then enters a loop where it controls the motors based on the distance readings. If the distance is below the threshold, it drives forward, otherwise it drives backward. The PWM duty cycle is calculated based on the distance and clamped to the range [0, 255]. The motors are controlled using the gpioWrite and gpioPWM functions from the pigpio library. The cleanup function is called on every exit path to ensure the motors stop and pigpio cleans up.

