This code assumes that the I2C device and GPIO chip are available and properly configured. It also assumes that the sensor's register layout and behavior match the Si1182-A-GM. It uses the Linux I2C-dev interface to communicate with the sensor and libgpiod to control the LED. It handles I2C errors with up to 3 retries and a 10 ms delay between attempts. It installs SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handlers for graceful cleanup: it turns off the LED, closes the I2C file descriptor, and closes the log file.

