This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up the GPIO pins, and installs a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM. It then enters a loop that reads the state of the buttons and updates the servo position accordingly. If the lock button is pressed, the servo is set to the locked position (2000 µs pulse width). If the unlock button is pressed, the servo is set to the unlocked position (1000 µs pulse width). The loop sleeps for 1 second after each update to avoid excessive CPU usage. The loop exits when the stop flag is set by the signal handler. When the loop exits, the servo is set to 0 (stop) and the pigpio library is terminated.

