This code initializes two GPIO chips, two motors, and two threads for each motor's encoder. The main control loop calculates the PID output for each motor, sets the PWM duty cycle, and logs the motor speed and PID values. The encoder threads monitor the quadrature encoder signals and update the motor's encoder count. The cleanup function releases the GPIO lines and closes the chips when the program is interrupted.

